<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">gryphon-rider-routes</ansi>

The Gryphon Rider lineage splits at level 10 into a heavy stoop that knocks
its foe down, a watcher on the wing or a venomous rider on a wyvern's hide.
None of the three asks anything of your alignment, at level 10 or at level
30. All three shape the Dive (<ansi fg="command">help gryphon-rider</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Gryphon Knight</ansi>

  10 Lance charge       a Dive with a two-handed reach weapon (a war spear)
                        knocks the foe down when it lands
  15 Plated barding     +4 armor
  20 Falling stone      a Dive deals 50% more damage (not on top of Power
                        dive: 50% in all)
  25 Steady wings       a Dive costs no Evasion

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Gryphon Lord</ansi> (30, <ansi fg="command">help gryphon-lord</ansi>): a Dive ready every other round.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Skyscout</ansi>

  10 Eagle eye          +6 Perception when your company looks for an ambush
                        in the open (not indoors)
  15 Quick stoop        Dive is ready a round sooner
  20 Hawk's mark        a Dive that lands leaves the foe exposed
                        (<ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>)
  25 Far sight          Eagle eye gives +12 Perception

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Falcon Marshal</ansi> (30, <ansi fg="command">help falcon-marshal</ansi>): allies strike harder at the foe it dove on.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Wyvern Rider</ansi>

  10 Venom stoop        a Dive that lands poisons the foe
  15 Wyvern hide        +8% maximum health
  20 Stinging tail      +2 Attack
  25 Wyvern guile       +3 Evasion

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Wyvern Lord</ansi> (30, <ansi fg="command">help wyvern-lord</ansi>): poisoned foes it dives on take more damage.

Elite classes are neutral and open to any alignment at level 30
(<ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>). Routes are final.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help gryphon-rider</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help ambush</ansi>.
